      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65972,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 427,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:34:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65973,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 427,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Superficial angiomyxoma arises in the dermis and/or superficial subcutis of the vulva.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:34:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65974,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 427,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Superficial angiomyxomas classically present as slow-growing, painless, and often exophytic lesions. Most are &lt;&nbsp;5&nbsp;cm {10435560; 9421071}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:34:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65975,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 427,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients are commonly of reproductive age {10435560; 9421071}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:34:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65976,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 427,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:34:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65977,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 427,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>If multifocal, superficial angiomyxoma can be a manifestation of Carney complex, which is an autosomal dominant disorder typically caused by <em>PRKAR1A</em> (17q24) mutations or less commonly by alterations of 2p16 {10973256; 8609225}. Carney complex encompasses a spectrum of skin pigmentation abnormalities, endocrine tumours or disturbances, myxomas, psammomatous melanotic schwannomas, and testicular large cell calcifying Sertoli cell tumours.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:34:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65978,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 427,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Superficial angiomyxoma is frequently polypoid, with a gelatinous, lobulated cut surface {10435560; 9421071}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:34:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65979,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 427,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Superficial angiomyxoma is characterized by a multinodular proliferation of well-delineated myxoid lobules composed of spindled and stellate cells and thin-walled curvilinear blood vessels {10435560; 9421071}. The cells, which have ovoid to round nuclei and delicate cytoplasmic processes, usually lack cytological atypia and mitotic activity and are often accompanied by an infiltrate of neutrophils. Although some tumours have an intermixed epithelial component (e.g. entrapped squamous epithelial nests or adnexal structures), there is no evidence of frank invasion into adjacent tissue {3389450}. Tumours are limited to the dermis and/or subcutis of cutaneous sites or the lamina propria of mucosal sites.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:34:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65980,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 427,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:34:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65981,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 427,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:34:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65982,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 427,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> involvement limited to superficial tissue; non-infiltrative growth; lobules of myxoid stroma with cytologically bland spindled to stellate cells; curvilinear vasculature; stromal neutrophils.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:34:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65983,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 427,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:34:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65984,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 427,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Approximately 30% of tumours recur {10435560; 9421071}. Complete excision reduces the risk of local, non-destructive recurrence.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:34:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
